WEBVTT

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>The year was 1889.</i>

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.980
<i>At sea, ship after ship met with tragedy due to sea monsters.</i>

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.320
<i>It was also the year the Paris World Exposition,</i>

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.740
<i>representing the cream of scientific civilization, was held.</i>

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:41.450
<i>Jean, who loves new inventions, befriended King, a baby lion,</i>

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.120
<i>and Nadia, a girl who is a circus performer.</i>

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>Nadia also possesses a marvelous gem called the Blue Water.</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.750
<i>An evil trio who want to steal this gem, kidnapped Nadia,</i>

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.130
<i>but Jean managed to rescue her unharmed.</i>

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.840
<i>Nadia and King can no longer return to the circus,</i>

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.970
<i>and have decided to go with Jean to Le Havre.</i>

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.850
<i>What is the secret that lies behind Nadia's Blue Water?</i>

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.260
Nadia, don't worry. They can't do anything now we're this far away.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.720
They must have given up by now.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.100
Don't worry so much!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.230
When we reach Le Havre, I'm sure Auntie will help us.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.940
I know.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:13.580
Catch up with those kids quickly!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.590
If we don't hurry, it's going to get dark.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.050
Leave it to me!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.300
Of all things, being pushed around by those kids.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.900
Nadia, if we could fly....

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.820
If you could really fly, where would you want to go?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.740
I...

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.490
I'd like to go back to the country where I was born.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.040
The country where you were born? Where's that?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.580
I don't know.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.920
Do you mean you've forgotten?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.880
Yes, I don't remember.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.680
But King keeps telling me it's Africa.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.760
I have a feeling he's right.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.640
But Africa is so far away,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.350
and it's so big.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.570
King wants to return to Africa too, don't you?

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.110
Africa?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.570
That is far away.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.000
King, what's the matter?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.460
What's that?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.170
What can it be?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.090
Amazing, a ship covered with iron plates!

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.890
But it looks familiar somehow.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.140
It's them! They've found us!

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.640
I knew it!

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.100
It flies through the air and floats on water. What a vehicle!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.610
Come on, we've got to get away!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.650
I guess you're right.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.190
Jean, they'll catch up with us!

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.400
Don't worry.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.000
Looks like they caught sight of us.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.870
It's too late for them.
They can't get away from us.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.420
Engines, full power!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.920
Aye, aye!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.070
We've got them now!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.530
The game is over. You'd better give up!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.280
Jean!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.620
Don't worry! I guess it's time to use our final weapon.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.740
Separation of aft section!

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.800
Hydrofoil ship Emeraude II, take off!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.430
That's unbelievable!

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.240
How's that? We must've left them miles behind.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.490
The foils lift the ship and lower water resistance.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.740
That's the secret to its speed.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.750
It's remarkable, Jean! What a great invention!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:42.210
I think so too. The idea belongs to another Frenchman.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.590
I just improved on it.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.590
To think a young boy like you could make an invention like this!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.600
I think I have a knack for mechanical things.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.600
Just incredible! You're a do-it-yourself genius!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.930
I'm better than that!

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.060
I'm sorry!

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.770
What's that?

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.200
What happened?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.700
The mechanism was not tested for endurance.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.700
But what went wrong?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:18.790
It just broke down.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.790
What a lousy invention!
And I thought it was so wonderful.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.630
I'm sorry.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.400
Is that another invention of yours?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.270
Yes, it's a flashlight.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:50.190
It has a small hand driven generator for power.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.660
It takes a lot of work though.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.990
It certainly does.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.090
This is Auntie's house.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:07.800
Wait just a minute.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.020
Oh, it's you, Jean.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.390
I'm home, Auntie.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.400
Welcome home. Where's your uncle?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.150
Uncle is still in Paris.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.030
Is that so?

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.530
Probably out living it up!

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.160
That lazy good-for-nothing!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.160
Auntie, there's a favor I want to ask of you.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:43.500
Could you take care of a young girl for a while?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.500
What did you say? Who is that child?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:52.880
We became acquainted in Paris. Bad guys were after her, and...

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.510
Jean, come inside.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.090
It won't take long.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.900
What is it?

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.860
Jean Rocque Raltique!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.730
Do you intend to take in a girl who is a complete stranger?

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:15.400
She's colored too. And on top of that, she has an ugly looking cat!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.870
Who knows what trouble they may cause!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.370
Nadia's not that kind of a girl!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.910
She must have you really fooled.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:29.090
Furthermore, Jean, do you intend to spend the money

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.960
my brother left you making a pile of junk?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.550
Of course not.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:37.680
You're spending money left and right on crazy inventions!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.720
This time I'm going to make it. I feel confident.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.100
You've got to be kidding!

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:47.060
Selling a farm to build an airplane that won't even fly! It's crazy!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.650
Now, you want to take care of that girl?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.780
There isn't much money left.
We have to keep some for schooling.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.530
Now you want to feed a girl, a colored girl,

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:03.410
and her big cat? Well, I refuse to help you!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.620
Excuse me, Auntie. I'll be back again. Bye!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.960
Wait, Jean! Wait, I said!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.420
Wait!

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.000
Nadia, wait!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.220
Why did you leave?

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.800
Thank you.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:23.140
But it's all right. I can take care of myself.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:28.560
Don't be like that. Just wait a moment. What's come over you?

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.480
I can't impose on you anymore.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.150
Goodbye.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:38.320
You're not imposing! Not at all!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.410
I know!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.290
Let's go to my house.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:49.920
Your house?

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:53.920
Yes, it's still quite early, and we'd be by ourselves there.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.310
We're very close now. Are you tired?

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:17.320
No, but it certainly is a long road.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.240
Eventually, this road will become a runway.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.160
A runway?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.160
That's right, a runway for an airplane.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.080
Whose grave is that?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.880
Etoile de la Seine I through VI are lying in that graveyard.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:43.050
Those are the iron graves of aircraft that could not take off.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.720
I see...

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.470
That's my house over there.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.600
It's quite strange.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.360
Yes, it's my pride and joy!

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.360
Good morning, Nadia.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.990
What?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.580
She must have left.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.560
Good morning, Nadia!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.730
You're an early riser.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:21.730
Good morning!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.110
I'll get the tea going. Wait downstairs.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:26.860
All right.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.290
This is quite a collection!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.830
You live here all by yourself?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:39.080
Yes, you see, my father was a sailor and rarely at home.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.960
He left some money for me with my uncle,

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.630
since a sailor can never tell what may happen to him.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:49.970
What a nice father!

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:55.430
So, Uncle and I can continue our inventions and studies.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.900
And these are your inventions?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:04.190
Yes. Of course, we made some mistakes.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:11.120
But one day I'll build an aircraft that can fly around the world.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.120
Around the world?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.580
Right! And I'm going to go look for my father.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.420
Your father?

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:24.000
Yes, my father was lost at sea a year ago while crossing the Atlantic,

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.300
along with his ship.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.510
Because of the sea monsters?

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.310
I'm sorry.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:39.520
Don't be! There's no real proof that the ship sank.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.900
That's true! I'm sure he's still alive and living somewhere.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:46.650
Of course he is! He's the best sailor in the world!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.950
Goodness, a moving stairway!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.870
I saw one at the Expo.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:01.380
Unfortunately, somebody was ahead of me in this.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:04.800
Now then, let me show you my great invention.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.590
It's upstairs.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.760
Here, step on.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.090
All right.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.100
Here I go.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.270
What happened?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.900
It broke down.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.610
Sorry! It was too weak to support two people.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.620
Another lousy invention, I think.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.080
I should've expected it.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.080
This is incredible!

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.130
Did you make this?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.800
This aircraft can fly through the skies.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:52.840
Aren't all aircraft supposed to do that?

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.680
Actually, no aircraft has really flown yet.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.930
Oh yeah, those six iron crosses in the graveyard, right?

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:02.810
I didn't mean those, I meant in the whole world.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.690
Oh, is that so?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:06.570
What's the name of your airplane?

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.110
Etoile de la Seine VIII.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.820
What happened to VII?

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.280
It sank in the Seine yesterday.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:17.280
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.160
I'm not! It was to rescue you!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.620
Thank you!

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:33.680
Oh?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.260
I've found her!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.180
You'd better not let her get away this time!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.140
Change! Land operation mode, switch on!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.190
Vertical mode!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.960
What's wrong, Nadia? You've been just standing here.

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.760
It's nothing.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.660
Nadia...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.030
Yes?

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.530
How much do you weigh?

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.540
Your weight?

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:47.040
How rude! How can you ask a lady such a question?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.420
Is that right?

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.920
You're hopeless. Anyway, I'm lighter than you.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.800
Really? That's great! Then it's all right.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.930
As I promised you, I'm going to take you into the skies.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.310
Let's fly to Africa together!

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:06.770
But...

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.780
Thank you.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.530
What can it be?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:17.610
I don't know.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.920
Hey, kids, you can't get away from me now.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.420
Give me the Blue Water!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.920
Or else something terrible is going to happen to you. I'm not fooling!

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.680
It's no use trying to hide! Give up!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.970
Sanson, teach them a lesson!

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:47.390
Yes, Ma'am! Stand by to fix on target!

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:48.390
Roger!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:54.360
Let's see. That should do it.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.610
Jean, what shall we do?

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.360
Get away in this.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.320
Fire!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.790
They've really started shooting at us!

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.090
Jean, are you sure you want to do this?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:18.470
Of course. I was planning to fly it with Uncle anyway.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.610
What are they trying to do?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.570
You're not going to get away like that!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.650
Why don't you just surrender?

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.250
I'm depending on you, my Etoile de la Seine!

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.750
Are you sure this will carry two people?

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.260
In theory, yes.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:12.730
Hey, what do you think you're doing?
I told you it's no use!

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.230
Take off!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:26.070
What's wrong? We're not flying!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.790
It has to gain enough speed to take off first.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.920
But we're just speeding over that long road.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.210
This is odd. The road should be long enough.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.670
We're going to crash!

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.220
Just a little more!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.430
It's useless I tell you! Stop right there!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:50.930
If you don't, I'm going to put a shell in you!

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:53.770
Leave it to me, please. I'll blow them to bits!

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.690
Climb!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.070
Sanson, who told you to fire?

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.740
It's flying!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.580
I can't believe this!

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.760
What a pair of kids!
I have to give them credit.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.380
But we have to do something.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.180
Sanson! Hanson! Let's go after them!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.180
Ain't that something!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.770
Come on, climb!

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.940
We made it! We made it! We're flying! We're really flying!

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:48.320
It's just as I calculated!
Nadia, see? We're flying!

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.830
This is amazing.
We're actually flying through the skies!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:55.580
Naturally! My theory is perfect.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:58.580
You're a true genius!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.590
We're going to fly straight to Africa!

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.170
Let's!

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:11.600
But maybe we'd better fly along the shore.

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.100
You may be right.

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:25.690
What's wrong?

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:29.240
I don't know. But something's wrong.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.120
What happened?

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.130
It broke down.

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:44.500
Not again! Can't you do something?

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:46.720
I'm trying to.

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:50.640
Your inventions are all lousy!

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:53.350
And I thought you were a genius.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:59.100
I'm sorry! I don't think we can make it to Africa.

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:01.100
You can't fix it?

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.000
We made it!

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:24.750
How long can we stay afloat?

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:28.010
Don't worry. We can stay afloat until help comes.

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.720
You see, it's completely waterproof.

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.550
You won't get wet this time!

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:42.100
Maybe not from the sea, but what about the rain?
